# Mount Carmel ERP — Backend Phase 1: Foundation

**Scope of this document:** the foundational backend that everything else plugs into — the auth engine, granular RBAC, school configuration, system settings, and the Super Admin dashboard — plus the real-time and background-job infrastructure the rest of the ERP will build on.

**Stack (locked):** Django + Django REST Framework · PostgreSQL · Django Channels + Redis (WebSockets) · Celery + Redis (background jobs) · JWT auth · S3/R2 storage · Paystack/Flutterwave (later phases).

**Frontend:** React PWA + Tailwind (already built). This backend serves it over REST + WebSockets.

---

## 1. Why "foundation first"

The spec describes ~17 roles and dozens of modules, but they all share four things: **who you are** (auth), **what you're allowed to do** (RBAC), **what the school is** (configuration), and **how the system behaves** (settings). Build these once, correctly, and every later module (students, finance, exams, hostel…) becomes a matter of adding models + endpoints + permission strings — not re-solving auth or access control each time.

The build order for Phase 1:

```
1. Project skeleton + settings + Postgres + Redis
2. Custom User model + JWT auth engine (+ OTP/2FA)
3. RBAC: permissions, roles, role_permissions, user_roles
4. DRF permission classes that read RBAC
5. School configuration + system settings
6. Real-time layer (Channels) + background jobs (Celery)
7. Audit logging (cross-cutting)
8. Super Admin dashboard (aggregation endpoints + live widgets)
```

