## 7. System settings

Configuration is *academic structure*; settings are *how the software behaves* — SMS/email credentials, payment-gateway keys, notification toggles, numbering formats. A flexible key/value store beats a rigid table here.

```python
# apps/settings_app/models.py
class SystemSetting(BaseModel):
    key = models.CharField(max_length=100, unique=True)  # "sms.provider", "payments.paystack.public_key"
    value = models.JSONField()                            # string, number, bool, or object
    group = models.CharField(max_length=50)              # "sms", "email", "payments", "numbering"
    is_secret = models.BooleanField(default=False)       # masked in API responses, encrypted at rest
```

**Groups & example keys**

| Group | Keys |
|---|---|
| `sms` | `sms.provider`, `sms.sender_id`, `sms.api_key`* |
| `email` | `email.host`, `email.from`, `email.password`* |
| `payments` | `payments.paystack.public_key`, `payments.paystack.secret_key`*, `payments.flutterwave.*` |
| `notifications` | `notifications.absentee_alert_enabled`, `notifications.channels` |
| `numbering` | `numbering.admission_format` (e.g. `MC/{year}/{seq:04}`), `numbering.receipt_format`, `numbering.invoice_format` |
| `result` | `result.pass_mark`, `result.show_position`, `result.lock_after_publish` |

`*` = `is_secret`: encrypted at rest, never returned in plaintext (write-only fields; responses show `••••`).

