## 9. Notifications & background jobs (Celery)

Sending SMS/email/WhatsApp/push, running the daily absentee sweep, generating overdue reminders — none of these should block an HTTP request. They run as **Celery tasks** on a Redis broker.

```python
# apps/notifications/models.py
class Notification(BaseModel):
    recipient = models.ForeignKey("accounts.User", on_delete=models.CASCADE, related_name="notifications")
    title = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    body = models.TextField()
    category = models.CharField(max_length=50)      # "payment", "attendance", "approval"...
    data = models.JSONField(default=dict)           # deep-link payload
    is_read = models.BooleanField(default=False)
    read_at = models.DateTimeField(null=True, blank=True)
```

```python
# apps/notifications/services.py
def dispatch(recipient, title, body, category, channels=("in_app",), data=None):
    n = Notification.objects.create(recipient=recipient, title=title, body=body,
                                    category=category, data=data or {})
    # 1) live push to the bell
    push_to_user(recipient.id, NotificationSerializer(n).data)
    # 2) external channels, async
    if "email" in channels: send_email.delay(recipient.id, title, body)
    if "sms"   in channels: send_sms.delay(recipient.id, body)
    if "push"  in channels: send_push.delay(recipient.id, title, body)
    return n
```

**Notification endpoints**

```
GET    /api/v1/notifications                 # ?unread=true
GET    /api/v1/notifications/unread-count
POST   /api/v1/notifications/{id}/read
POST   /api/v1/notifications/read-all
```

**Scheduled tasks (Celery Beat)** — foundation-level ones:
- nightly cleanup of expired OTP challenges and blacklisted tokens
- (hooks reserved for later phases: absentee sweep, overdue-fee reminders, payroll runs)

