## 10. Audit logging (cross-cutting)

The spec is firm: sensitive actions (result edits after publish, fee refunds, permission changes) must be traceable. Audit logging is not a module you visit — it's a service every other module calls.

```python
# apps/audit/models.py
class AuditLog(BaseModel):
    actor = models.ForeignKey("accounts.User", null=True, on_delete=models.SET_NULL)
    action = models.CharField(max_length=100)     # "result.published", "role.permissions_changed"
    target_type = models.CharField(max_length=100, blank=True)  # "Student", "Role"
    target_id = models.CharField(max_length=64, blank=True)
    changes = models.JSONField(default=dict)       # {"before": {...}, "after": {...}}
    ip_address = models.GenericIPAddressField(null=True)
    user_agent = models.CharField(max_length=300, blank=True)

class LoginHistory(BaseModel):
    user = models.ForeignKey("accounts.User", null=True, on_delete=models.SET_NULL)
    successful = models.BooleanField()
    ip_address = models.GenericIPAddressField(null=True)
    user_agent = models.CharField(max_length=300, blank=True)
```

```python
# apps/audit/services.py
def log(actor, action, target=None, changes=None, request=None):
    AuditLog.objects.create(
        actor=actor, action=action,
        target_type=target.__class__.__name__ if target else "",
        target_id=str(getattr(target, "id", "")),
        changes=changes or {},
        ip_address=_ip(request), user_agent=_ua(request),
    )
```

**Audit endpoints** (gated `audit.view`, Super Admin/Principal):

```
GET /api/v1/audit/logs           # filter by actor, action, date range, target
GET /api/v1/audit/login-history
```

Audit logs are **append-only** — no update/delete endpoints exist, by design.

