## 11. Super Admin dashboard

The dashboard is an **aggregation layer**, not new data — it reads across modules and returns summary numbers, then keeps the volatile ones live over the WebSocket.

Because most Phase-1 modules (students, fees, exams) don't exist yet, the dashboard is built so each widget degrades gracefully: a service function per widget that returns `0`/empty until its module lands, then starts returning real figures. This lets you ship the Super Admin shell now and have the numbers "wake up" as later phases arrive.

### Widgets (from spec Sections 2 & 36)

```
Statistics:   students, teachers, staff, parents, classes
Financial:    fees_collected, outstanding_fees, todays_payments
Academic:     present_today, absent_today, upcoming_exams, pending_results
Operations:   inventory_alerts, library_activity, hostel_occupancy, transport_status
Feed:         recent_activities (from audit log), announcements
```

### Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/dashboard/summary` | All top-line counters in one call |
| GET | `/api/v1/dashboard/financial` | Fees collected / outstanding / today |
| GET | `/api/v1/dashboard/academic` | Attendance today, upcoming exams, pending results |
| GET | `/api/v1/dashboard/recent-activity` | Latest audit-log entries (paginated) |

```python
# apps/dashboard/services.py  (illustrative)
def build_summary():
    return {
        "students": Student.objects.filter(is_deleted=False).count() if _has("students") else 0,
        "teachers": Teacher.objects.count() if _has("teachers") else 0,
        "staff":    Employee.objects.count() if _has("hr") else 0,
        "parents":  User.objects.filter(user_type="parent").count(),
        "classes":  SchoolClass.objects.count(),
        # ...volatile ones (present_today, fees_collected) also pushed live via WS
    }
```

**Live behavior:** when a payment is recorded or attendance is submitted (later phases), the responsible service calls `push_to_role("super_admin", {...})`, and the dashboard widget updates in place. Phase 1 wires the plumbing; the events attach as modules land.

Dashboard access is gated by `dashboard.view`; Super Admin sees the full board, and later roles (Principal, Accountant) get filtered variants of the same endpoints via their permission set.

