## 12. Security checklist (Phase 1)

The foundation is where security is won or lost — every later module inherits it.

- **Passwords** hashed with Argon2 (Django's `PASSWORD_HASHERS`).
- **JWT** short-lived access (~15 min) + rotating refresh, refresh blacklist on logout.
- **2FA/OTP** hashed, single-use, 5-minute expiry, rate-limited.
- **RBAC** enforced at the DRF permission layer on every endpoint — no endpoint ships without an explicit permission mapping.
- **Secrets** (`is_secret` settings) encrypted at rest, never returned in plaintext.
- **Rate limiting** on auth endpoints (login, OTP, password reset) via DRF throttling.
- **CORS** locked to the PWA origin; **CSRF** enforced on any cookie-based paths.
- **SQL injection / XSS** — ORM + DRF serializers by default; never raw string SQL.
- **Audit trail** on every sensitive mutation; login history on every attempt.
- **Session management** — list/revoke device sessions from `/auth/sessions`.
- **Input validation** centralized in serializers; standard exception handler so errors never leak stack traces.

