[ ] configuration: models + set-current-session service + endpoints
[ ] settings_app: key/value store + secret encryption + endpoints
[ ] audit: models + service + middleware + login history
[ ] realtime: ASGI + Channels + Redis layer + JWT ws-auth + consumer
[ ] notifications: model + dispatch service + Celery channel tasks
[ ] celery + beat: broker wired, cleanup tasks scheduled
[ ] dashboard: aggregation services + endpoints + live-push hooks
[ ] seed default roles (spec §33) with their permission bundles
[ ] security pass: throttling, CORS, Argon2, secret masking
```

Once this foundation is in, every later module (students → academics → finance → hostel → transport → …) is: add app → models → serializers → viewset with a permission mapping → register any new permission strings → optionally emit notifications/audit/live-push. No auth or access-control rework required.

