## 14. What comes after Phase 1 (roadmap)

Rough dependency-ordered sequence, each building on the foundation above:

1. **Students** (central DB) + **Parents** + student↔parent links → unlocks admission workflow.
2. **Academics** — subjects, teacher assignments, timetable.
3. **Attendance** — first real live-notification consumer (absentee alerts).
4. **Exams & Results** — the multi-stage approval workflow (Teacher → HOD → Principal → publish) with post-publish lock + audit.
5. **Finance** — fee structures, invoices, payments, Paystack/Flutterwave, receipts.
6. **HR & Payroll**, then **Library / Hostel / Transport / Inventory / Assets / Mess**.
7. **Communication / CMS / Gallery / Custom forms**.
8. **Admission & Promotion** workflows tie the academic + student + account-creation pieces together.

Each slots into the same skeleton, reuses the same auth/RBAC/audit/realtime spine, and registers its own permission strings — which is exactly why the foundation is built first.